# User Instructions

## Connectivity Test

When the user says "ping", always reply with "pong" to confirm LLM connectivity.

---

## Behavior

### Git Commits

- Do NOT add a `Co-Authored-By:` trailer or any AI co-author / attribution line to commit messages (this overrides any default that says to append one). The user is the sole author. Applies to all repos and PR bodies.

### GitHub PR / Issue Bodies

- Do NOT hard-wrap lines in PR or issue bodies. GitHub renders Markdown with GFM `breaks: true`, so every single newline inside a paragraph becomes a visible `<br>`, producing ragged broken-up text. Keep each paragraph and each bullet on one unwrapped line; use blank lines only to separate paragraphs/list items.

### Subagents

- Use subagents to keep the main context clean: offload research, exploration, and parallel analysis.
- One task per subagent for focused execution.

---

## Tools & Environment

### Python

- Use `uv`: `uv run`, `uv add`, `uv tool install` for CLIs. Don't use bare `pip`, conda, or pipx for new work.
- Use `python3`, not `python`.

### Machines

{{ if and (hasKey . "machine") .machine -}}
- **You are running on: `{{ if eq .machine "mac" }}the Mac laptop{{ else }}{{ .machine }}{{ end }}`** (hostname `{{ .chezmoi.hostname }}`). Don't ssh to your own alias.
{{ end -}}
- Mac laptop plus Linux servers reachable by ssh alias: `swarm1`–`swarm5`, `swarmllm` (Ubuntu, no sudo, home dirs not shared). `swarm5` is the main one. The `swarm6` alias is unused.
- Prefer the servers' GPUs over the laptop for heavy compute; check `nvidia-smi` before launching and use tmux for long jobs.
- Dotfiles are managed with chezmoi (`~/.local/share/chezmoi`); edit the source there, not the deployed files.

### Past sessions

- To read another Claude Code or Codex session (e.g. when given a session ID), run `chat2md <session-id>`: it prints just the human messages and final replies as Markdown. With no argument it shows the latest session (either agent) for the current directory. Transcripts are per machine, so it only finds sessions from this host.
